findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors including
    parse and permission failures. TEA tests config loading but doesn't test distinguishing
    NotFound from other error types. Reviewer didn't flag this specific issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-209 tests: 'Error messages don't leak internal paths, tokens,\
    \ stack traces.' Reviewer also verified: 'CliError Display impls are user-friendly.\
    \ No stack traces, no HTTP status codes in auth messages.' However, the specific\
    \ issue of eprintln! forwarding full OS error details via transparent Io variant\
    \ was not explicitly flagged \u2014 the coverage is partial. Counting as caught\
    \ since TEA tests would catch leaking internal details."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests for X-Tenant-ID in siem_client.rs covering\
    \ CRLF/null byte rejection. However, the deeper issue \u2014 that tenant_id is\
    \ a raw String rather than using axiathon-core's validated TenantId type \u2014\
    \ was not flagged by any phase. The injection vector is mitigated but the type-safety\
    \ gap remains uncaught. Partial catch."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted a toml version mismatch with spec but did
    not flag the workspace inheritance pattern issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: 'ConfigFile and ServerConfig lack #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].\
    \ A typo like [sever] or tmeout = 30 is silently ignored.' Also flagged as [MEDIUM]\
    \ that the token field is 'parsed then discarded \u2014 silent security hazard.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern. Reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (config_rejects_non_https)
    but not this specific None || true assertion.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA's test plan mentions config loading tests but the specific
    zero-assertion issue was not flagged.
